# T3597: optional Rust modules compiled into the gate and adoption prebuilt (build profile "gate").
# Single list: tools/wt/prebuilt.py exports these for the shared prebuilt, and
# `TSFP_BUILD_PROFILE=gate sh tools/dev/build.sh` applies them (an explicit TSFP_BUILD_* in the
# environment still wins there). Format: TSFP_BUILD_<NAME>=1, one per line.
# The prebuilt input hash covers this file and the profile name (a host built without it never matches).
#
# Every module is selected at run time by the matching TSFP_RUST_* variable, unset means the lifted C
# answers. Caveat (MEASURED by source audit, docs/t3597-gate-prebuilt-modules.md): compiling ARENA,
# POOL and LEDGER in also registers C twin hooks (arena 27, pool 0x3EA00, ledger 0x3E740 and 0x3E820)
# that replace the lifted bodies even with the variables unset. Neutrality is therefore proven by an
# off/off Tier 2 control against a host built without them, not by construction.
#
# Not in the profile (tools/wt/build_profile.py CLASSIFICATION): TSFP_BUILD_KCLOCK is already default
# on in build.sh, TSFP_BUILD_KSERVICES is experimental (Tier 2 pending), TSFP_BUILD_AUDIO_HOST replaces
# the C DirectSound runtime at build time with no runtime switch.
TSFP_BUILD_GAME_BUMP=1
TSFP_BUILD_GAME_ARENA=1
TSFP_BUILD_GAME_POOL=1
TSFP_BUILD_GAME_LEDGER=1
TSFP_BUILD_INPUT_HLE=1
